\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang1040\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. All hail the power of Jesu's name;
\par Let angels prostrate fall;
\par Bring forth the royal diadem
\par To crown Him Lord of all.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Crown Him, ye martyrs of our God,
\par Who from His altar call;
\par Extol Him in whose path ye trod,
\par And crown Him Lord of all.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Ye seed of Israel's chosen race,
\par Ye ransomed from the fall,
\par Hail Him who saves you by His grace,
\par And crown Him Lord of all.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Sinners! Whose love can ne'er forget
\par The wormwood and the gall;
\par Go spread your trophies at His feet,
\par And crown Him Lord of all.
\par \pard\fi720 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Let every tribe and every tongue
\par Before Him prostrate fall,
\par And shout in universal song
\par The crowned Lord of all.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. O that with yonder sacred throng
\par We at His feet may fall,
\par Join in the everlasting song,
\par And crown Him Lord of all! 
\par \lang1033\f1 
\par \cf1\lang1040\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

